{#-
  OVHcloud Object Storage lifecycle policy for the MariaDB backup bucket.
  Applied by mariadb-backup-s3-init.sh via `s3api put-bucket-lifecycle-configuration`.

  This policy EXPIRES objects. It deliberately does not transition them: the
  upload scripts already PUT backup sets and rotated binlogs straight into the
  Infrequent Access class, so a transition rule would have nothing useful left
  to do — and it would actively cause harm. Lifecycle transitions fire on object
  age, not on write activity, and an S3 prefix filter is a literal string that
  cannot express "*/sets/ but not */binlogs/" (the host component comes first,
  and the policy is bucket-wide because every db host applies the same one). So
  any transition rule here also covers the ACTIVE binlog, which is deliberately
  kept in Standard because it is overwritten every 5 minutes and each overwrite
  counts as a delete against IA's 30-day minimum. On an idle DB the sync skips
  the unchanged active binlog, the object ages past the transition, and every
  later overwrite then buys the early-deletion charge the design exists to
  avoid. See mariadb-binlog-sync.sh.

  Expiration is therefore the whole job, and it is the ONLY thing that deletes
  old backups — the scripts never remove remote data. Objects are in IA from the
  moment they land, and IA is billed for a 730h (30 day) MINIMUM per object with
  early deletion charged for the remainder, so expire_days is clamped below to at
  least min_storage_days.

  Rule 2 aborts orphaned multipart uploads. A full backup is a single multi-GB
  streamed multipart upload; if it dies mid-flight the uploaded parts are billed
  but invisible to `s3 ls`, so this rule is what stops them accumulating.

  NoncurrentVersionExpiration is a safety net for a bucket that has versioning
  turned on against the advice in pillar/private/init.sls.example. A bucket
  without versioning may not echo it back, which mariadb-backup-s3-init.sh's
  --check accounts for.
-#}
{%- set backup = salt['pillar.get']('mariadb:backup', {}) %}
{%- set s3 = backup.get('s3', {}) %}
{%- set lc = s3.get('lifecycle', {}) %}
{%- set prefix = s3.get('prefix', '').strip('/') %}
{%- set filter_prefix = (prefix ~ '/') if prefix else '' %}
{%- set min_storage_days = lc.get('min_storage_days', 30)|int %}
{%- set expire_days = [lc.get('expire_days', 35)|int, min_storage_days]|max %}
{%- set abort_days = lc.get('abort_incomplete_multipart_days', 7)|int %}
{
  "Rules": [
    {
      "ID": "mariadb-backups-expiry",
      "Status": "Enabled",
      "Filter": { "Prefix": "{{ filter_prefix }}" },
      "Expiration": { "Days": {{ expire_days }} },
      "NoncurrentVersionExpiration": { "NoncurrentDays": {{ expire_days }} }
    },
    {
      "ID": "mariadb-backups-abort-incomplete-uploads",
      "Status": "Enabled",
      "Filter": { "Prefix": "{{ filter_prefix }}" },
      "AbortIncompleteMultipartUpload": { "DaysAfterInitiation": {{ abort_days }} }
    }
  ]
}
